  (text "Remote: all COM terminals to GND, NO1-NO4 to J5 pins 3-6.\n+12 V board shown; power a 5 V board from +5V instead." (at 190.5 238.76 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid eb584e35-a355-595c-a89b-0f7e0e240517)
  )
  (text "INTERFERENCE AND RELIABILITY MEASURES" (at 279.4 177.8 0)
    (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 0dfadc70-0d06-5d09-a519-e4f2be7a051b)
  )
  (text "1. D2 flyback diode right at the valve terminals (stripe to +).\n2. Valve current has its own wire pair (J2) back to J1: star ground at J1.\n3. Decoupling: C1 + C2 on 12 V, C3 + C4 at U1, C12 at the Nano, C6 at J4.\n4. Flow input: R1 10k pull-up, R2 1k + C5 10nF filter, firmware glitch filter.\n5. Button and remote inputs: 10k pull-ups + 100nF, firmware debounce.\n6. F1 fuse + D1 crowbar protect against shorts and a reversed supply.\n7. R11 / R12 divide the 5 V data line down to 3.2 V for the ESP.\n8. Twist each sensor / remote signal with its GND; route away from valve wires.\n9. Ground plane on the PCB bottom layer; keep the 12 V valve tracks short and wide." (at 279.4 181.61 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 00ab8b5b-b1d5-5777-99b8-b56af7f5a6c2)
  )

